module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.Completion.KoszulAdicCompletionLimit
public import StacksFrontier.Homology.DerivedCategory.InverseSystem.DerivedLimitProIso
public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# The derived completion is the derived limit of the derived adic quotients, Tag 0A0K (1)

Let `Y` be a quasi-compact locally Noetherian scheme, let `ℐ ⊂ 𝒪_Y` be the quasi-coherent sheaf
of ideals generated by global sections `f_1, …, f_r` of `𝒪_Y`, and let `K` be an **arbitrary**
object of `D(𝒪_Y)`. Then

`K^∧ = R lim (K ⊗^𝐋_{𝒪_Y} 𝒪_Y/ℐⁿ)`,

which is part (1) of [Stacks, Tag 0A0K].

## How the proof goes

`R lim` is a predicate rather than a functor
(`CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated.IsDerivedLimit`), so the assertion is that the object `K^∧` *is*
a derived limit of the tower `n ↦ K ⊗^𝐋 𝒪/ℐⁿ`; nothing has to be said about a comparison map,
and that is why this part needs no canonical identification where part (3) does.

Two inputs meet, and the whole point is that they meet **after** the coefficient object has been
factored out of the tower:

* [Stacks, Tag 0A0E] presents `K^∧` as a derived limit of `n ↦ K ⊗^𝐋_𝒪 (K^n)^∨` for an arbitrary
  `K`; this is `isDerivedLimit_tensorDerivedDualSystem_koszulPowerSystem_completion` in the
  namespace `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite`. That tower is
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.tensorDerivedDualSystem`, which is **by definition** the dual
  Koszul tower followed by the functor `K ⊗^𝐋 -`.
* The dual Koszul tower itself — no coefficients — is pro-isomorphic to the tower `n ↦ 𝒪/ℐⁿ` in
  degree zero. This is `Stacks.Algebraization.koszulAdicProIso` read at the coefficient sheaf
  `𝒪_Y`, which is coherent because `Y` is locally Noetherian
  (`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherenceCriteria.structureSheaf_isCoherent`), composed with the
  identification of the coefficient-free tower inside the coefficient one.

A pro-isomorphism of towers is carried along any functor
(`InverseSequence.ProIso.whiskerRight`), so applying `K ⊗^𝐋 -` to the second input turns the
tower of the first into the tower of the conclusion, for every `K` at once. No associativity or
unit constraint of the derived tensor product is needed: the coefficient enters both towers as
the *same* whiskering functor.

The last step is `CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated.IsDerivedLimit.of_proIso` of
`Homology/DerivedCategory/InverseSystem/DerivedLimitProIso.lean`: being a derived limit of a tower
is a property of the object, and it transfers across a pro-isomorphism of towers because a derived
limit of the second tower exists and [Stacks, Tag 0H9L] identifies it with the given one.

## Where the coefficient-free tower comes from

`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.tensorDerivedDualSystem X T F E` is
`F.op ⋙ (dual) ⋙ T.tensor.obj E`, so at `E = 𝒪` in degree zero it is the dual tower whiskered by
`𝒪 ⊗^𝐋 -`. Removing that whiskering is exactly
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.koszulTensorDualSystemIso` at `E = 𝒪`: its target
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedSheafHomSystem X F 𝒪` is the dual tower on the nose. So the
unit constraint of the derived tensor product is not needed either — the comparison of
[Stacks, Tag 0BYU] already supplies that one instance of it.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Algebraization.koszulDualDerivedSystemIsoShifted` — the dual Koszul tower is the
  shifted dual Koszul tower with coefficients in `𝒪_Y`.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.proIso_koszulDualDerivedSystem_adicQuotientSystem` — the dual Koszul
  tower is pro-isomorphic to `n ↦ 𝒪_Y/ℐⁿ` in degree zero.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.isDerivedLimit_derivedTensor_adicQuotientSystem_completion` —
  **part (1) of [Stacks, Tag 0A0K]**.

## The hypotheses, and what they are for

`[CompactSpace Y]` is genuine and enters in exactly one place: the Artin–Rees level behind the
pro-vanishing of the Koszul cohomology sheaves below the top degree is produced one per member of
an affine cover and the proof maximises over a *finite* cover
(`Stacks.KoszulProZero.exists_koszulPowerComplexOnDown_homologyMap_eq_zero_of_coherent`).
Pro-vanishing of a tower of *sheaves* is not a local condition — a map of sheaves vanishes when it
vanishes on a basis, but the level at which it does is produced chart by chart — so no localization
removes it from this route. The source avoids it by working with the canonical map
`K ⟶ R lim (K ⊗^𝐋 𝒪/ℐⁿ)` of [Stacks, Remark 52.6.13] and concluding by locality of
invertibility; the module documentation of `Completion/AdicQuotientDerivedLimit.lean` records
what that route needs.

`[IsLocallyNoetherian Y]` is the tag's own hypothesis and is used for the same Artin–Rees input,
together with the coherence of `𝒪_Y` that it supplies. The source's `ℐ` is an arbitrary
quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals, and here it is the one generated by `f_1, …, f_r`: that is the
scope in which the Koszul tower of [Stacks, Tag 0A0E] exists on `Y` itself. Nothing is lost by
fixing the ideal sheaf to `Stacks.Algebraization.koszulIdealSheafData`, because an `IdealSheafData`
is determined by its affine components and so every ideal sheaf generated by those sections equals
it — `Stacks.Algebraization.eq_koszulIdealSheafData`.

The object `K` carries no hypothesis at all: it ranges over the whole of `D(𝒪_Y)`, as in the
source.

## Implementation notes

The derived category is taken with `CategoryTheory.HasDerivedCategory.standard`, the instance
[Stacks, Tag 0A0E] is stated with, and the `HasProduct`/`HasCoproduct` data that lets a derived
limit be written down at all is produced by `inferInstanceAs` at the `Y.Modules` spelling of the
category of modules, as in `Completion/KoszulAdicCompletionLimit.lean`: the site's
`SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)` and `Y.Modules` are
definitionally but not reducibly equal, and instance search succeeds only at the second.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A0E](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A0E)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A0K](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A0K)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BYU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BYU)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0H9L](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0H9L)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated
open Opposite

universe u

attribute [local instance] AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.submoduleCompleteLattice

namespace Stacks.Algebraization

attribute [local instance] modulesEnoughInjectives HasDerivedCategory.standard

section Main

open scoped IsMulCommutative


variable (Y : Scheme.{u}) [IsLocallyNoetherian Y] [CompactSpace Y] {r : ℕ}
  (f : Fin r → Presheaf.globalSections
    ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf).O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{u}))

/-- **The dual Koszul tower of `D(𝒪_Y)` is the `r`-fold shift of the dual Koszul tower with
coefficients in `𝒪_Y`.**

Both sides are the tower of [Stacks, Tag 0A0E] at the coefficient object `𝒪_Y` in degree zero:
on the left the coefficient has been removed by
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.koszulTensorDualSystemIso`, whose target is the dual tower itself,
and on the right it has been absorbed into the Koszul complex with coefficients by
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.koszulTensorDualSystemCoefficientIso`. -/
def koszulDualDerivedSystemIsoShifted :
    RingedSite.derivedSheafHomSystem (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf)
        (RingedSite.koszulPowerSystem (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) f ⋙
          DerivedCategory.Q)
        (RingedSite.derivedStructureSheaf
          (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf)) ≅
      koszulShiftedDualDerivedTower Y f
        (SheafOfModules.unit
          (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf
            (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf).O)) :=
  (RingedSite.koszulTensorDualSystemIso (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) f
      (RingedSite.derivedStructureSheaf
        (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf))).symm ≪≫
    RingedSite.koszulTensorDualSystemCoefficientIso
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) f
      (SheafOfModules.unit
        (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf
          (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf).O))

/-- **The dual Koszul tower is pro-isomorphic to the tower `n ↦ 𝒪_Y/ℐⁿ` in degree zero**, for
`ℐ` the quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals generated by `f_1, …, f_r`.

This is `Stacks.Algebraization.koszulAdicProIso` at the coefficient sheaf `𝒪_Y` — coherent
because `Y` is locally Noetherian — preceded by
`Stacks.Algebraization.koszulDualDerivedSystemIsoShifted`, which removes the coefficient from the
tower. -/
def proIso_koszulDualDerivedSystem_adicQuotientSystem :
    InverseSequence.ProIso
      (RingedSite.derivedSheafHomSystem (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf)
        (RingedSite.koszulPowerSystem (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) f ⋙
          DerivedCategory.Q)
        (RingedSite.derivedStructureSheaf
          (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf)))
      (adicQuotientSystem (koszulIdealSheafData Y f)
          (SheafOfModules.unit
            (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf
              (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf).O)) ⋙
        DerivedCategory.singleFunctor Y.Modules 0) :=
  haveI : (SheafOfModules.unit Y.ringCatSheaf).IsCoherent :=
    Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherenceCriteria.structureSheaf_isCoherent Y
  CategoryTheory.Pro.proIsoTrans
    (InverseSequence.ProIso.ofNatIso (koszulDualDerivedSystemIsoShifted Y f))
    (koszulAdicProIso Y f (SheafOfModules.unit Y.ringCatSheaf) (koszulIdealSheafData Y f)
      (koszulIdealSheafData_ideal Y f))

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0A0K, part (1).** Let `Y` be a quasi-compact locally Noetherian scheme,
let `ℐ ⊂ 𝒪_Y` be the quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals generated by the global sections
`f_1, …, f_r`, and let `K` be an arbitrary object of `D(𝒪_Y)`. Then the derived completion `K^∧`
of `K` along `ℐ` is a derived limit of the tower `n ↦ K ⊗^𝐋_{𝒪_Y} 𝒪_Y/ℐⁿ`:

`K^∧ = R lim (K ⊗^𝐋_{𝒪_Y} 𝒪_Y/ℐⁿ)`.

`R lim` is a predicate rather than a functor here, exactly as in the tag's part (4)
`Stacks.Algebraization.isDerivedLimit_single_limit_powerQuotients`, so the source's equality is
read as the object `K^∧` being a derived limit of the tower; no comparison map has to be
produced, and nothing is weakened by that reading.

The proof is [Stacks, Tag 0A0E] — `K^∧` is a derived limit of `n ↦ K ⊗^𝐋 (K^n)^∨` — together
with the pro-isomorphism of the dual Koszul tower with `n ↦ 𝒪/ℐⁿ`, whiskered by `K ⊗^𝐋 -`. The
coefficient object enters both towers as that same whiskering functor, so the two meet with no
constraint of the derived tensor product used.

`[CompactSpace Y]` is a genuine hypothesis of this route and not an artefact: the Artin–Rees
level behind the pro-vanishing of the Koszul cohomology sheaves below the top degree is produced
one per member of an affine cover and the proof maximises over a *finite* cover. See the section
"The hypotheses, and what they are for" of this file. The source asks neither for
quasi-compactness nor for `ℐ` to be globally generated; `Completion/AdicQuotientDerivedLimit.lean`
records what a proof at the source's own hypotheses would take. -/
@[stacks 0A0K "part (1), `K^∧ = R lim (K ⊗^𝐋_𝒪 𝒪/𝓘ⁿ)`: for an **arbitrary** object `K` of \
`D(𝒪_Y)` on a quasi-compact locally Noetherian scheme `Y` and the quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals \
`𝓘` generated by global sections `f_1, …, f_r` of `𝒪_Y`, the derived completion `K^∧` along `𝓘` \
is a derived limit of the tower `n ↦ K ⊗^𝐋_{𝒪_Y} 𝒪_Y/𝓘ⁿ`. `R lim` is a predicate rather than a \
functor, so the source's equality is read as `K^∧` being a derived limit of that tower, which is \
the same reading the tag's part (4) is registered with. The ideal sheaf is the extension to `Y` \
of the ideal those global sections span, so its generation by them is a definition and not a \
hypothesis, and every ideal sheaf so generated equals it. The object `K` carries no hypothesis"]
theorem isDerivedLimit_derivedTensor_adicQuotientSystem_completion
    (K : DerivedCategory Y.Modules) :
    IsDerivedLimit
      ((adicQuotientSystem (koszulIdealSheafData Y f)
            (SheafOfModules.unit
              (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf
                (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf).O)) ⋙
          DerivedCategory.singleFunctor Y.Modules 0) ⋙
        (Stacks.SheafOfModules.canonicalDerivedTensorProduct
          (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf)).tensor.obj K)
      ((RingedSite.completionFunctor
        (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) f).obj K) := by
  have hco : HasCoproduct
      ((RingedSite.koszulPowerSystem (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) f ⋙
        DerivedCategory.Q).obj) :=
    inferInstanceAs (HasCoproduct (show ℕ → DerivedCategory Y.Modules from
      (RingedSite.koszulPowerSystem (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) f ⋙
        DerivedCategory.Q).obj))
  exact IsDerivedLimit.of_proIso
    (InverseSequence.ProIso.whiskerRight
      (proIso_koszulDualDerivedSystem_adicQuotientSystem Y f)
      ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.canonicalDerivedTensorProduct
        (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf)).tensor.obj K))
    (RingedSite.isDerivedLimit_tensorDerivedDualSystem_koszulPowerSystem_completion
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) f K)

end Main

end Stacks.Algebraization

end
